package SyspresentDecisions {
    doc /* Owner-agreed product and architecture direction, 19 October 2026. Decisions describe intended behavior; they do not establish implemented capability or verification evidence. */
    comment semanticRuntime /* OpenSysML Go is the semantic engine, hosted as WASM in a browser worker and natively in CI. Syspresent owns a new interactive canvas through a versioned semantic/view adapter. The VS Code extension source is not a dependency of the new canvas architecture. Keep OMG repository access as a possible future adapter rather than a required backend. */
    comment graphVersusModel /* A scoped view projection is not the complete model graph. Keep model identity, diagram representation identity, scene intent, calculated layout and transition correspondence distinct. Preserve behavior-specific information from native processing; never reconstruct engineering meaning from labels. */
    comment dynamicCanvas /* The graph canvas is the primary interface in both standalone exploration and guided stories. Every scene may rearrange freely for visibility; semantic identity and reader focus persist rather than global coordinates. Settled scenes remain steady while read. Active content controls fit and centering; translucent one-hop engineering context occupies only peripheral space and never enlarges the active fit bounds. */
    comment narrativeSpace /* Floating Markdown panels are measured layout occupants. Their size and placement may change between scenes and viewport sizes; the diagram layout must account for their actual area. Panel anchors express semantic association without forcing the panel to move on every node movement. */
    comment journeys /* Same-notation changes with shared semantic content gather, fade and relayout directly. Disjoint same-notation contexts also use a GV journey. Use one continuous animation clock across intermediate viewpoints rather than separately eased stop-and-start stages. Entering and leaving nodes, relationships and narrative fade. A departing tile vacates a replacement region by moving off frame and fading before the replacement enters; exit sweeps avoid retained tiles and prose or fade before contact when blocked. Held arrivals start smoothly. Scheduling applies within each adjacent viewpoint interval and preserves intermediate native waypoint visibility. Cross-notation transitions pass through GV, travel meaningful engineering relationships, gather the destination features and morph into the new notation. Automatic journeys ascend actual directed engineering links to the nearest common ancestor, then descend. Native project ownership provides a separately labeled location fallback; it is not engineering derivation. Each journey shows bounded local windows and retains native edge directions. No permitted ancestor means a disclosed explicit jump. Proposed routes are author-editable and saved explicitly, and invalid saved routes fail validation for every diagram type. The presentation declares a system of interest with scene additions; shared KerML or library ancestry never creates an automatic shortcut. */
    comment modelViews /* Reusable selection belongs in SysML view definitions and usages with native executable semantics. Markdown references those views and owns narrative, scene order, emphasis and transition choreography. Do not duplicate a model query/traversal language in Markdown. Rendering intent in SysML does not itself implement JavaScript layout or animation. */
    comment readerInteraction /* First click, tap or keyboard selection highlights and reveals contextual actions. Only an explicit action changes focus or expands the graph. Departing a guided scene collapses prose into Return to scene; returning restores its authored viewpoint and content. */
    comment requirementQuestions /* Statement, rationale, origins, system impact and verification are questions answered through diagram compartments, annotations and selected relationships. The rejected separate requirement-question reader is not the default architecture. Preserve explicit definition-to-usage typing and native relationship direction. */
    comment authoring /* Editing mode runs on the static site. Authors import a project, explore and capture viewpoints, edit narrative and views, and export ordinary files or a ZIP. Underlying system model authoring is deferred; authored view definitions remain editable. Markdown can also be imported or exported independently. */
    comment coverage /* Include the complete project by default. Explicit scoped publications remain supported and disclose unavailable targets separately from hidden content. Stories guide loaded-model traversal without becoming hard exploration barriers. */
    comment snapshots /* Preserve immutable story, model, evidence and runtime snapshots. Rebuild validation reports broken references; deep change history, automatic semantic adjudication and mandatory reapproval on model updates are not current work. Existing catalog lifecycle records do not establish engineering approval. */
    comment notation /* Preserve the broad product notation requirements: structure, requirements, activities, sequences, states, fault trees and native tables. A small GV-to-other-notation prototype proves the new contract without claiming complete notation support or replacing the reader study. Multiple regions may coexist with visible notation boundaries. */
    comment generalViewOrder /* General structural views place classifiers and general definitions above typed usages and specializations by default, preserving native arrows. Source requirements appear above derivations or refinements; satisfying parts and verifying cases appear below their requirements. Visual decision-chain rank does not assert model ownership. Authored constraints may adjust this. Behavioral and fault-tree views retain their semantic ordering. */
    comment scopedMilestone /* The immediate milestone proves real native/WASM identity and view parity, focused engineering traversal, a GV gather-to-other-notation transition, measured Markdown space and capture/export of a scene using an unrelated small model. This is a prototype milestone, not completion of the earlier whole-product goal. */
    comment connectionRouting /* Use ELK as a disposable joint geometry engine in a browser worker, with native OpenSysML identities and relationship endpoints unchanged. Structural siblings may stagger or change order for readability; behavior concurrency and actual model ports retain their native meaning. Display anchors are not model ports. Relationship selection traces its route and endpoints without rearranging the scene. Prefer short low-bend structural routes using the actual facing sides, while reserving distinct native terminals and measured labels. Translucent context routes participate in crossing and overlap minimization against active corridors and each other. Preserve active geometry; try peripheral rerouting and alternate positions before short continuations, and disclose residual conflicts. Each peripheral continuation has its own labeled route and marker; never merge distinct relationships into an apparent junction. Revalidate moving connection paths against tile obstacles and their current endpoints instead of interpolating through tiles or leaving floating wires. Invisible routes have no pointer or keyboard targets. */
    comment focusedRequirementTraversal /* Requirement selection offers directional origins, derived requirements, system impact and verification actions on the existing canvas. Traverse actual native links with at most one explicit requirement definition/usage typing bridge. Bounded result pages disclose their limits; missing projected links do not prove model absence. Back and Forward restore focus, native view, scene handoff, expanded statements and presentation preferences. Display preferences in Markdown control compartments, edge emphasis, peripheral budget and soft sibling ordering by actual owner, without replacing native selection or inventing containment. */
    comment focusedStructure /* Parts and packages default to structural context ahead of competing requirement traces. Display native composition for parts and separately labeled ownership for package declarations. A part usage may expose parts declared on its direct type through one visible typing bridge, preserving declaration identities and never expanding sibling usages or type ancestry. Parts / contents and Containing element actions are directional and bounded; native peer connections between selected contents remain visible. Requirement defaults remain engineering-focused. */
    comment deferred /* Underlying system-model editing, shared accounts/collaboration, a required backend, deep model history, automatic model diffs and mandatory change-review workflows are deferred. Full-product notation coverage, complete portable-project editing and human usability acceptance require separate evidence beyond the prototype. */
}
